.TH AQUALIZER 1 "2026-08-09" "aqualizer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aqualizer \- audio output equalizer for PipeWire
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aqualizer
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Aqualizer
inserts a ten\-band equalizer into PipeWire's audio path and provides ready\-made
presets such as Bass, Vocal and Acoustic.
Run with no arguments it opens a GTK window; the commands below give the same
access without a graphical interface.
.PP
Signal processing uses PipeWire's built\-in biquad filters, so no extra DSP
library is required. The chain configuration is written to
.I ~/.config/pipewire/filter-chain.conf.d/99-aqualizer.conf
and loaded by
.BR filter-chain.service .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the insertion mode, target device, active preset and every band value.
.TP
.B list
List the built\-in presets and your own.
.TP
.BI set " PRESET"
Apply a preset, for example \fBaqualizer set bass\fR.
.TP
.BI bands " DB ..."
Set all ten bands by hand, from 31 Hz up to 16 kHz.
.TP
.B on\fR, \fBoff
Turn the equalizer on or bypass it without removing it.
.TP
.B devices
List output devices, noting which mode each one requires.
.TP
.BI device " NAME"
Pin the output to one device, or \fBauto\fR to follow the default device.
.TP
.BI save " NAME"
Save the current band settings as a preset of your own.
.TP
.B install\fR, \fBuninstall
Install the chain into PipeWire, or remove it and restore audio as it was.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-apply\-only
Reapply the saved preset and exit, without opening the GUI. Used by
.BR aqualizer.service .
Does nothing when the user has never used Aqualizer or has turned it off.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH INSERTION MODES
Aqualizer chooses between two ways of inserting itself into the audio path.
.TP
.B smart
The node is marked as a smart filter and WirePlumber inserts it on its own
between applications and the device in use. The real device stays visible in the
sound settings.
.TP
.B sink
The node becomes a virtual sink that is made the default output, with its own
output pinned to the real device. Used for devices that are themselves smart
filters \(em in practice, Bluetooth devices \(em because smart mode would never
be traversed there.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aqualizer/state.json
Active preset, band values, device and mode.
.TP
.I ~/.config/aqualizer/presets/
Your own presets, in JSON.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pipewire/filter-chain.conf.d/99-aqualizer.conf
The generated filter\-chain configuration. Do not edit it by hand; it is
rewritten every time a preset changes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pw\-cli (1),
.BR pw\-dump (1),
.BR wpctl (1),
.BR libpipewire\-module\-filter\-chain (7)
